defect c7-III-02LE-machine-header D10 maps:src:D.2.38 Remove the machine status/dependency header and print the small tag; preserve every permanent identity.
defect c7-III-02LE-smooth-types D27 maps:src:D.2.38 Refine maps:src:D.2.38 under the same identity. OS56(3,10), zero4,e=1 has actual mod2 cube0 and integral mu0; the old conic connected sum has cube1 and mu5 gamma3(s), fixed under every unit action u^3. OS56(1,10),zero1,e=1 has odd p1 pairing -42=3 mod5 and refined coefficient2, whereas old epsilon is0. The complete replacement is X=M_(1+kappa mod2)#Z_(p,epsilon), P_p=(b/p-a nu)/2, P_(2p)=CRT(1+kappa,P_p), mu=p(1+kappa mod2)gamma3(s). All twelve patterns stand; mod2 assignments3,4,5,6,7,9,10 and odd assignments1,4,5 change. There are three order-ten types with multiplicities2,4,1 and two order-fourteen types with multiplicities3,2.
defect c7-III-02LE-physical-fan-cube D25 maps:eq:D.MP4 Retain the integral physical polynomial and both true period differences. The actual prescribed fan has short basis SC, with phi(Cv)=-psi(v)+L0 v and integral L0=(a row1(C)-epsilon)/2. The reciprocal monomials identify regular Cartier frames including all units. C^-1 delta=(-b kappa,nu), c_C=(b/2)(a kappa(b kappa-nu)-1)=1+kappa mod2, degree a(nu-b kappa). D.MP7 is therefore cube1+kappa, not uniformly1.
defect c7-III-02LE-common-action-normalization D25 maps:eq:D.MP8 The physical action has cusp pair +/-nu and elliptic pair +/-w. The exponent nu^-1 with inverse nu changes both pairs to +/-1 and +/-w/nu. In z[C]=1 marking, z[Ep]=-w^2/nu^2 and z p1=-2(1-w^2/nu^2); its coefficient (w^2/nu^2-1)/2 converts by a nu to P_p=(b/p-a nu)/2. All physical w values stand; the old zero criterion omitted this common action map.
defect c7-III-02LE-line-comparison D22 maps:src:D.2.38 Supply the actual theta, Gaussian and integral monomial gauges with reciprocal inverses, all h/F/J maps and units. The degree-one graph and primitive exterior maps prove torsion-free H^2(V); the exact global line has Omega and zero sweep values. The tensor-square/cap comparison proves the original two-torsion bound by the stronger exact Chern equality.
defect c7-III-02LE-borel-character-choice D22 maps:src:D.2.38 Give the whole-circle-fixed endpoint, split actual fundamental group, unique finite subgroup, complete degree-two kernel and common base shift with inverse. Retain the mixed integral degree-one term; its square vanishes. The shift comparison stands but its actual cusp character is 1+kappa.
defect c7-III-02LE-coefficient-inverses D22 maps:src:D.2.38 The full CW homotopy equivalence stands. Give its cellular retraction q with qi=id and iq~id relative wedge; CRT inverse p x+(1-p)y; bordism inverse factor inclusions followed by inverse CRT; unit inverse p+(1-p)r^-1; connected-sum ball contraction, neck collapse and oriented spin one-handle map. The preceding Phi and Phi^-1 give the exact primitive second-homology marking.
defect c7-III-02LE-certificate-prose D09 maps:src:D.2.38 Remove historical certificate/execution assertions. The proof states the complete factor, component and cap-option method and all resulting patterns. The new raw-only computation and post-exposure auxiliary checks are separately retained/read; no historical LE certificate was opened or credited.
defect c7-III-02LE-recognition-locus D18 maps:src:D.2.38 Specify Theorem5 p796 injection, Theorem3 p795 and Section4.1 p809 marked zero-free-H3 construction and uniqueness. Both free H2 and H3 ranks vanish here; preserve the admitted K9 printed-rank correction. The diffeomorphism induces Phi and its inverse induces the stated inverse. No additional primary or whole-PDF reading is claimed.
